  "description": "Maps burn scars, surfaces which have been sufficiently affected by fire to display significant changes in the vegetation cover (destruction of dry material, reduction or loss of green material) and in the ground surface (temporarily darker because of ash). Monthly datasets are available at global scale, in the spatial resolution of 300 m, and with a time lag of two months. They cover the period from 2019 to 2025.",
